lesson: 226
title: How long it takes on the clock
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To find how long something lasts, count on from the start time to the next o'clock, then on to the end time.
explain: An hour has 60 minutes, so from a quarter past to the next o'clock is 60 − 15 = 45 minutes.
explain: From 3:45 to 4:30: 15 minutes to 4:00, then 30 more, so 15 + 30 = 45 minutes.
vars: a=name h=1..10 p=2..10 q=2..11
let: s = 5 * p
let: e = 5 * q
answer: 60 - s + e
exercise: A lesson starts at {h}:{s} and ends at {h+1}:{e}. How many minutes long is the lesson?
exercise: {a} leaves home at {h}:{s} and gets to {a.his} aunt's house at {h+1}:{e}. How many minutes is the journey?
exercise: A train leaves at {h}:{s} and arrives at {h+1}:{e}. How long is the trip in minutes?
exercise: {a} starts painting at {h}:{s} and stops at {h+1}:{e}. For how many minutes does {a.he} paint?
exercise: The swimming party runs from {h}:{s} to {h+1}:{e}. How many minutes does it last?
exercise: got on the bus {h}:{s}, off at {h+1}:{e}. how long was i on it, in minutes
exercise: {a} started homework at {h}:{s+5}, no wait {h}:{s}, done at {h+1}:{e}. how many mins
exercise: film {h}:{s} til {h+1}:{e}, popcorn was {p} quid lol. how many minutes
exercise: {a} reckons {h}:{s} to {h+1}:{e} is {100-s+e} minutes. that right? how many
exercise: footy practice {h}:{s} to {h+1}:{e}, how long
exercise: How many minutes are there from {h}:{s} to {h+1}:{e}?
test: How many minutes pass between {h}:{s} and {h+1}:{e}?
test: The clock said {h}:{s} when {a} fell asleep in the car and {h+1}:{e} when {a.he} woke up. For how many minutes did {a.he} sleep?
test: Bread goes into the oven at {h}:{s} and comes out at {h+1}:{e}. For how many minutes does it bake?
test: {h}:{s} to {h+1}:{e} how many mins
test: left {h}:{s} got there {h+1}:{e}, traffic was mad. mins?
test: The shop opened its doors at {h}:{s}; by {h+1}:{e} it had sold {q+10} cakes. How many minutes after opening was that?
exam: Determine the number of minutes which elapse between {h}:{s} and {h+1}:{e} on the same day.
exam: A railway service departs at {h}:{s} and arrives at its destination at {h+1}:{e}. Ascertain the duration of the journey in minutes.
exam: It is given that an instructional session commences at {h}:{s} and terminates at {h+1}:{e}. State its duration in minutes.
exam: Compute the interval, expressed in minutes, between the commencement of an activity at {h}:{s} and its cessation at {h+1}:{e}.
exercise: {a} said {a.he} was "just popping to the loo" at {h}:{s} and came back at {h+1}:{e}. How many minutes was {a.he} gone?
exercise: dad said he'd "just pop to the pub for one" at {h}:{s}. rolled in at {h+1}:{e}. how many minutes was "one" lol
test: The head called the fire drill "a minor inconvenience". It began at {h}:{s}, and everyone was back inside at {h+1}:{e}. For how many minutes were the children outside?
